  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.5 — New features\n• app.UseSinkSharp() — one-line middleware: X-Correlation-Id lifecycle + ElapsedTime stopwatch\n• WriteTo(sink, minLevel) — per-sink minimum log level independent of global minimum\n• WithDashboard(out sink, minLevel) — per-sink level for dashboard sink\n• WithMachineName() — standalone MachineName enricher, zero runtime cost\n• WithRequestId(accessor) — stamps RequestId from HttpContext.TraceIdentifier (Web API only)\n• WithUserContext(accessor) — stamps UserId, UserName, UserRole; safe for anonymous endpoints (Web API only)\n• WithRequestPath(accessor) — stamps HttpMethod + RequestPath (Web API only)\n• WithElapsedTime(accessor) — stamps ElapsedMs since request start; needs app.UseSinkSharp() (Web API only)\n• .Filter(predicate) — drop events before enqueue; zero allocation for dropped events; all project types\n• .WithEnricher(enricher, when: predicate) — conditional enrichment; enricher skipped when predicate is false\n• SinkSharpLoggerFactory.SetGlobalLevel(level) — change minimum level at runtime, no restart needed\n• AddSinkSharpRequestId() / AddSinkSharpUserContext() / AddSinkSharpRequestPath() / AddSinkSharpElapsedTime() DI helpers\nv1.0.4 — Bug fixes\n• DisposeAsync() is now idempotent — no ObjectDisposedException on second call\n• Phone regex uses lookbehind/lookahead — correctly matches (555) 123-4567\nv1.0.1 — Bug fix: email regex corrected\nv1.0.0 — Initial release: striped async queue, MessageTemplate caching, object pool, PII masking, correlation ID, MEL compatible\nSee full changelog: https://github.com/SinkSharp/CHANGELOG.md",
